    "narrative": "The Zurich Zebras enter today\u2019s slate with a high-ceiling lineup, anchored by **Pete Crow-Armstrong** (82.13) and **Junior Caminero** (77.68). **Pete Crow-Armstrong** is our premier play, benefiting from a prime leadoff spot and a high-leverage matchup against a righty with a slow delivery, which maximizes his elite speed profile in our SB-starved scoring environment. **Junior Caminero** also projects as an elite start, taking advantage of a favorable park factor and a strong platoon split against the right-handed Barnett. **Yordan Alvarez** (73.27) remains a must-start despite an inherent L/L disadvantage, as his elite xwOBA effectively negates the matchup concerns against the soft-tossing Whisenhunt.\n\nOur outfield is bolstered by significant platoon edges for **Lars Nootbaar** (67.77) and **Christian Yelich** (67.68), both of whom are projected to thrive against right-handed starters today. While **Dillon Dingler** (47.64) and **Caleb Durbin** (44.54) represent our most marginal starts, they remain in the lineup to preserve our game caps given the limited upside elsewhere. The most difficult personnel decision involved **Carson Benge** (49.17), who narrowly missed the starting nine; despite a favorable matchup, his lower efficiency compared to the high-OBP targets like **Kyle Schwarber** (62.04) and **Trea Turner** (65.12) necessitated his move to the bench. \n\nRisks are relatively contained today, though we are monitoring **Caleb Durbin** closely, as he faces a formidable test against Cease, whose sub-3.00 xERA creates a clear negative delta for our batting average categories. We have successfully avoided the basement, with **Jacob Gonzalez** (39.13) correctly benched for falling below our 40.0 efficiency floor, and **Kazuma Okamoto** remains sidelined, keeping our active rotation focused on high-efficiency, speed-oriented producers.",
